From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] jscript: JSON toJSON and array replacers, script errors for bad input, localeCompare, isView, GetObject(path, class)

Several JScript built-ins were E_NOTIMPL stubs, and bad input failed
with a bare E_FAIL that scripts cannot catch by type: web pages, HTAs
and installer scripts got "unspecified error" where Windows throws a
SyntaxError, TypeError or URIError that their try/catch expects.

- JSON.stringify uses a value's toJSON(key), and Date has toJSON (the ISO
  string, or null for an invalid date); an array replacer lists the
  member names to write (strings and numbers, each once, in order); a
  circular value throws TypeError 5034 "Circular reference in value
  argument not supported". A host object a reviver returns is kept.
- JSON.parse of bad text throws SyntaxError (1014 "Invalid character",
  1015 for an unterminated string); a value that is not a number is no
  longer read as 0.
- decodeURI and decodeURIComponent of bad escapes throw URIError 5025.
- Function.prototype.apply with an argument list that is not an array or
  arguments object throws TypeError 5028; null and undefined mean no
  arguments. Function.prototype() returns undefined; calling an arguments
  object is "Function expected".
- String.prototype.localeCompare compares in the user's locale.
- ArrayBuffer.isView is true for a DataView.
- Object.prototype.toLocaleString on a host object calls its toString.
- GetObject(path, class): no path gives the running object of the class,
  an empty path a new one, a file a new one that loads it.

Wine's jscript tests: run 102761, jscript 1734, caller 690, activex 919
tests, no failures, as before.

Gate: test/jsstubs-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit script host,
test/jsstubs-probe.c). Mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_TOJSON,
SG_MUTANT_NO_PROP_LIST (jscript/json.c), SG_MUTANT_URI_E_FAIL
(jscript/global.c).
